nce":0.8055,"shared":21,"play_caller":"Liam Coen"}],"defense":[{"season":2022,"team":"DEN","distance":0.4687,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Ejiro Evero"},{"season":2025,"team":"CAR","distance":0.7315,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Ejiro Evero"},{"season":2025,"team":"NO","distance":0.7805,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Brandon Staley"},{"season":2023,"team":"JAX","distance":0.9096,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"GB","distance":0.9349,"shared":22,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Rams went 5-12 in 2022 and were outscored 384 to 307. Neither side held up, as the offense ranked 29th in EPA per play and the defense 24th in EPA allowed. What set them apart was the highest 11 personnel usage and the highest Cover 3 rate in the league.","offense":"The Rams offense struggled, ranking 25th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Their biggest outliers in how they lined up were the highest 11 personnel usage and the 3rd lowest 12 personnel usage in the league. Matthew Stafford ran the passing game, with Tyler Higbee leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Rams defense was well below average by EPA allowed per play. It was much better against the run than the pass, ranking 11th and 26th. Aaron Donald was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Bobby Wagner, who had 6 sacks, after not being a regular on this defense last season. In terms of scheme, they had the highest Cover 3 rate in the league.","special":"The Rams were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 93% of field goals, which was one of the best in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the quarterback, about 18% of the money on the books. Their offensive line was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Matthew Stafford played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 2,087 yards. Targets were spread around, with Tyler Higbee and Cooper Kupp leading a group where nobody took more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield was a committee led by Cam Akers and Darrell Henderson. On defense, Leonard Floyd led the team with 9 sacks and Jalen Ramsey picked off 4 passes.","coaching":"Sean McVay called the offense as head coach and Raheem Morris called the defense. Their offense looked most like the 2022 and 2025 Vikings, both under Kevin O'Connell. Their defense looked most like the 2022 Broncos and the 2025 Panthers, both under Ejiro Evero.","trends":"The offense went from 8th in EPA per play in 2021 to 29th in 2022, a big step back. The defense moved from 11th in EPA allowed per play in 2021 to 24th in 2022, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was I formation usage, which went from 1% to 7%.","notes":"2022 is the first season with every data source available, including FTN's play design charting. It is also the last season that used the older formation labels, so singleback and I formation rates still appear here."}}